## NIT

### 44. no-useformaction-for-relative-posts

**Severity:** NIT

**Tempting:**
```tsx
<Form method="post" action="/users/123/edit">...</Form>
```

**Why wrong:** Hardcoding the route path breaks when the route file is moved or renamed. `useFormAction()` resolves the current route's URL.

**Canonical:**
```tsx
import { Form, useFormAction } from "react-router";
const action = useFormAction();  // resolves to current route
<Form method="post" action={action}>...</Form>
```

Source: https://reactrouter.com/api/hooks/useFormAction

